{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Then</b> — He likened the adversary to a sweeping wadi." "<b>The word נחלה</b> — in three ways, and all differ. For נחלה לישראל עבדו: the ḥet has a sheva naḥ and a pataḥ, and the he is a feminine marker, like the pattern of נחלה, a past verb from the nifʿal binyan, with under the ḥet a sheva alone, and the word is milraʿ. נחלה: the ḥet with sheva and the word is milʿel, for the accent is on the nun and the he is added like the he in לילה; therefore he said עבר, and the accent is double." "<b>And the meaning of חיים</b> — it refers back to the speakers, as if he said 'he swallowed us and we [were] alive,' as in 'they went down alive to Sheol' (Numbers 16:33)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 124, :notes {1 "The three interpretations are compressed and heavily grammatical; the text references Psalms 124:3 phrases (נחלה, עבר) and possibly Numbers 26:54 (לישראל עבדו). The phrase 'והטעם כפול' at the end is obscure — taken hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:18.212147764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}